{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.ZeqNRhoCorrection","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.ZeqNRhoCorrection","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring","lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.QIntegerCanonical"],"declarations":19,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.zeqN_at_one_via_q_correction","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.zeqN_at_one_via_q_correction","kind":"theorem","line":140,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/ZeqNRhoCorrection.lean#L140-L149","doc":"The finite-q form reduces to the integer Kashaev law at `q = 1`.\nCombines `zeqN_finite_q_form` with `qIntBal_one` and a small\nalgebraic rearrangement.  Independently of the `classical_limit`\nfield, this confirms the two class fields are consistent. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.zeqN_finite_q_form","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.zeqN_finite_q_form","kind":"theorem","line":129,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/ZeqNRhoCorrection.lean#L129-L138","doc":"The conjectural finite-q form: `B(q) = m_e · Vol · (ρ + A − [A]_q)`.\nDirect consequence of the `q_correction` field of the typeclass.\nThis is the formula whose empirical match at `10⁻³` precision on\n`²H, ⁴He, ¹²C, ¹⁶O` is documented in the audit. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.zeqN_at_one_eq_classical","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.zeqN_at_one_eq_classical","kind":"theorem","line":120,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/ZeqNRhoCorrection.lean#L120-L127","doc":"At `q = 1`, the conjectural binding energy reduces to the\ninteger Kashaev law.  Direct consequence of the\n`classical_limit` field of the typeclass. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.dimensionalAnomaly_at_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.dimensionalAnomaly_at_one","kind":"theorem","line":112,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/ZeqNRhoCorrection.lean#L112-L118","doc":"At `q = 1`, the dimensional anomaly vanishes — the q-deformation\ncorrection has no effect, and the Kashaev law is exact. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.qIntBal_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.qIntBal_one","kind":"theorem","line":108,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/ZeqNRhoCorrection.lean#L108-L110","doc":"`qIntBal 1 n = (n : ℝ)` by definition (the `if q = 1` branch). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.dimensionalAnomaly","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.dimensionalAnomaly","kind":"def","line":102,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/ZeqNRhoCorrection.lean#L102-L106","doc":"The dimensional anomaly `A − [A]_q` of the natural\n`U_q(sl_2)`-representation `V^(A-1)` controls the magnitude of\nthe substrate-q correction.  Vanishes at `q = 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.zeqNBindingEnergy","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.zeqNBindingEnergy","kind":"def","line":95,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/ZeqNRhoCorrection.lean#L95-L100","doc":"The conjectural binding energy for a Z=N atom at the substrate\nparameter `q`, lifted from the typeclass. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.ZeqNRhoCorrection.q_correction","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.ZeqNRhoCorrection.q_correction","kind":"theorem","line":91,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/ZeqNRhoCorrection.lean#L91-L91","doc":"**The conjecture itself**: the binding energy at finite `q` equals\nthe Z=N substrate-q-corrected form.  This is the field that\nplays the role of `sorry` for the conjecture. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.ZeqNRhoCorrection.classical_limit","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.ZeqNRhoCorrection.classical_limit","kind":"theorem","line":86,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/ZeqNRhoCorrection.lean#L86-L86","doc":"**Classical limit**: at `q = 1` recovers the integer Kashaev law. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.ZeqNRhoCorrection.bindingEnergy","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.ZeqNRhoCorrection.bindingEnergy","kind":"def","line":84,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/ZeqNRhoCorrection.lean#L84-L84","doc":"The binding energy at substrate `q`, predicted by the formula. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.ZeqNRhoCorrection.m_e","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.ZeqNRhoCorrection.m_e","kind":"def","line":82,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/ZeqNRhoCorrection.lean#L82-L82","doc":"Mass of the electron in MeV — a numerical constant. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.ZeqNRhoCorrection.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.ZeqNRhoCorrection.mk","kind":"ctor","line":80,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/ZeqNRhoCorrection.lean#L80-L80","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.ZeqNRhoCorrection","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.ZeqNRhoCorrection","kind":"class","line":58,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/ZeqNRhoCorrection.lean#L58-L93","doc":"**Z=N ρ-correction conjecture (axiomatised).**\n\nEncodes the assertion that for `Z = N = k` light atoms, the\nbinding-energy formula at finite substrate `q` takes the form\n\n`B(q) = m_e · Vol_hyp(K_A) · (ρ_struct + A − [A]_q)`.\n\nThe class is parametrised by the atom mass number `A` (the\nconjecture's empirical regime is the doubly-symmetric `A = 2k`\nline; the class itself does not enforce evenness — downstream\ncallers should restrict to even `A` or supply a separate\n`Even A` hypothesis) and the canonical knot assignment `K_A`.\nInstances supply:\n- `bindingEnergy q` — the binding energy at substrate q.\n- `classical_limit` — recovery of the integer Kashaev law at\n  q = 1.\n- `q_correction` — the conjectural finite-q form.\n\nThe `q_correction` field is the **conjectural input**: providing\nit is the role of mathematicians (not Lean).  Downstream\ntheorems consuming `[ZeqNRhoCorrection A K]` are conditional on\nit. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:conj:z-eq-n-rho-correction","label":"conj:z-eq-n-rho-correction","md":"quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/z-eq-n-rho-correction.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.qIntBal","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.qIntBal","kind":"def","line":49,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/ZeqNRhoCorrection.lean#L49-L56","doc":"q-integer `[n]_q = (q^n − q^(−n))/(q − q^(−1))`.  Specialises\nto `n` at `q = 1` (after applying l'Hôpital). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.KnotAssignment.vol_hyp_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.KnotAssignment.vol_hyp_pos","kind":"theorem","line":47,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/ZeqNRhoCorrection.lean#L47-L47","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.KnotAssignment.vol_hyp","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.KnotAssignment.vol_hyp","kind":"def","line":46,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/ZeqNRhoCorrection.lean#L46-L46","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.KnotAssignment.rho_struct","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.KnotAssignment.rho_struct","kind":"def","line":45,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/ZeqNRhoCorrection.lean#L45-L45","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.KnotAssignment.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.KnotAssignment.mk","kind":"ctor","line":44,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/ZeqNRhoCorrection.lean#L44-L44","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.KnotAssignment","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.KnotAssignment","kind":"structure","line":40,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/ZeqNRhoCorrection.lean#L40-L47","doc":"A canonical knot / link assignment for an `A`-host atom.\nConcretely a placeholder; in a fully-developed framework this\nwould carry the SnapPy data + the integer Wedderburn-block\nmultiplicity `ρ_struct`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}